WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.378
<v Examiner>The female reproductive system.

2
00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:04.013
<v Examiner>Ten marks.

3
00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:09.476
<v Examiner>Label all the structures of the female reproductive system, and state their functions.

4
00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:15.266
The other half of her ten-mark question, from her Repro Female deck and her quiz keys.

5
00:00:15.266 --> 00:00:20.855
Her figure is a front view, numbered one to eight: the vagina, the cervix, the myometrium,

6
00:00:20.855 --> 00:00:25.201
the cavity of the uterus, the fallopian tube, the fimbriae, the ovary,

7
00:00:25.201 --> 00:00:26.443
and the endometrium.

8
00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:27.995
Picture it as you listen.

9
00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:31.164
The hook: make, catch, carry, grow, deliver.

10
00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:35.675
The ovaries make the eggs, the fimbriae catch them, the tubes carry them,

11
00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:39.197
the uterus grows the baby, and the vagina is the way out.

12
00:00:39.647 --> 00:00:43.714
The system's function: to produce the female gametes, the ova;

13
00:00:43.714 --> 00:00:47.845
to secrete the female sex hormones, oestrogen and progesterone;

14
00:00:47.845 --> 00:00:51.125
and to support fertilisation, pregnancy and birth.

15
00:00:51.575 --> 00:00:56.257
The ovaries: paired, one on each side of the uterus, held by ligaments,

16
00:00:56.257 --> 00:00:58.566
and supplied by the ovarian artery.

17
00:00:58.566 --> 00:01:02.259
The follicles sit in the outer part, the ovarian cortex.

18
00:01:02.259 --> 00:01:07.205
Each follicle is an oocyte, an immature egg, surrounded by granulosa cells.

19
00:01:07.205 --> 00:01:11.756
The ovaries produce the eggs, and secrete oestrogen and progesterone.

20
00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:16.307
The fallopian tubes, also called the uterine tubes.

21
00:01:16.307 --> 00:01:18.132
One end opens into the uterus.

22
00:01:18.132 --> 00:01:22.631
The other widens into the ampulla, and ends in a funnel, the infundibulum,

23
00:01:22.631 --> 00:01:24.638
fringed with fingerlike fimbriae.

24
00:01:24.638 --> 00:01:27.192
The tube doesn't actually touch the ovary:

25
00:01:27.192 --> 00:01:32.057
the ovulated oocyte lands in the peritoneal cavity, and the fimbriae draw it in.

26
00:01:32.057 --> 00:01:36.435
The tube's jobs: to receive the oocyte, to be the site of fertilisation,

27
00:01:36.435 --> 00:01:40.996
and to carry the oocyte toward the uterus, by peristalsis and by its cilia,

28
00:01:40.996 --> 00:01:42.881
which help the sperm along too.

29
00:01:43.331 --> 00:01:46.645
The uterus: a hollow, thick-walled organ in the pelvis,

30
00:01:46.645 --> 00:01:49.416
behind the bladder and in front of the rectum.

31
00:01:49.416 --> 00:01:54.297
Its parts are the fundus, the rounded top above the tubes; the body; the isthmus,

32
00:01:54.297 --> 00:01:58.756
the narrow part; and the cervix, the neck, which projects into the vagina.

33
00:01:58.756 --> 00:02:03.576
Its function: it receives the embryo, and nourishes it until the placenta forms.

34
00:02:04.026 --> 00:02:06.562
The wall of the uterus has three layers.

35
00:02:06.562 --> 00:02:09.415
The perimetrium, the thin outer serous layer.

36
00:02:09.415 --> 00:02:14.678
The myometrium, the thick middle layer of smooth muscle, which contracts in labour.

37
00:02:14.678 --> 00:02:18.863
And the endometrium, the lining, rich in blood vessels and glands.

38
00:02:18.863 --> 00:02:24.506
Its stratum functionalis is shed in each period, and its stratum basalis grows a new one.

39
00:02:24.956 --> 00:02:30.012
The cervix: the neck of the uterus, with the cervical canal running through it,

40
00:02:30.012 --> 00:02:32.572
from the internal os to the external os.

41
00:02:32.572 --> 00:02:37.180
Its glands make mucus that blocks bacteria spreading up from the vagina.

42
00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.651
The vagina: a thin-walled tube from the cervix to the outside,

43
00:02:42.651 --> 00:02:45.764
with the urethra in front and the rectum behind.

44
00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:51.536
It's the passageway for birth and for menstrual flow, and the female organ of copulation.

45
00:02:51.536 --> 00:02:54.908
It's normally acidic, which keeps bacteria in check.

46
00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:59.707
Her quiz: antibiotics can kill off those bacteria, and let yeast overgrow.

47
00:03:00.157 --> 00:03:02.324
The external genitalia, the vulva.

48
00:03:02.324 --> 00:03:05.510
The mons pubis, the fatty pad over the pubic bone.

49
00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:10.099
The labia majora, the hair-covered outer folds, which match the scrotum.

50
00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:12.902
The labia minora, the hair-free inner folds.

51
00:03:12.902 --> 00:03:16.089
And the clitoris, erectile tissue under a prepuce.

52
00:03:16.089 --> 00:03:19.976
Her key: the clitoris is the female match to the glans penis.

53
00:03:20.426 --> 00:03:23.827
The breasts, the mammary glands, are modified sweat glands.

54
00:03:23.827 --> 00:03:26.421
They have their own track, with Pania's case.

55
00:03:26.871 --> 00:03:27.570
The traps.

56
00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:32.184
The endometrium receives the embryo; the myometrium is the muscle.

57
00:03:32.184 --> 00:03:36.378
Fertilisation happens in the fallopian tube, not the uterus.

58
00:03:36.378 --> 00:03:40.503
And the oocytes sit in the ovarian cortex, not the medulla.

59
00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:41.556
<v Examiner>Once more.

60
00:03:41.556 --> 00:03:44.089
<v Examiner>The female system, structure by structure.

61
00:03:46.539 --> 00:03:50.713
The ovaries hold the follicles in their cortex, make the oocytes,

62
00:03:50.713 --> 00:03:53.218
and secrete oestrogen and progesterone.

63
00:03:53.218 --> 00:03:57.328
The fimbriae of the fallopian tubes draw in the ovulated oocyte;

64
00:03:57.328 --> 00:03:59.769
the tube is the site of fertilisation,

65
00:03:59.769 --> 00:04:03.429
and cilia and peristalsis carry the oocyte to the uterus.

66
00:04:03.429 --> 00:04:09.145
The uterus, with its fundus, body, isthmus and cervix, receives and nourishes the embryo.

67
00:04:09.145 --> 00:04:14.412
Its wall is the perimetrium, the myometrium of smooth muscle, and the endometrium,

68
00:04:14.412 --> 00:04:17.815
whose functionalis is shed and whose basalis regrows.

69
00:04:17.815 --> 00:04:20.063
The cervix's mucus blocks bacteria.

70
00:04:20.063 --> 00:04:24.687
The vagina is the birth canal and the copulation organ, and it's acidic.

71
00:04:24.687 --> 00:04:29.504
The vulva is the mons pubis, the labia majora and minora, and the clitoris.
